Here is the complete fix:

---

## Summary

**Root Cause:** The `Util.getPreferences()` method used a hardcoded preference filename (`"org.moire.ultrasonic_preferences"`) instead of the app's actual default preferences file. In debug builds, the app ID is `org.moire.ultrasonic.debug` (due to `applicationIdSuffix ".debug"`), so `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences()` creates a different file (`org.moire.ultrasonic.debug_preferences`). When `ServerSettingsFragment` saves server credentials using `getDefaultSharedPreferences()` and `MusicServiceFactory` reads them using the hardcoded filename, they access different files — credentials appear null, and the fallback to `http://localhost` is triggered.

**Fix:** Changed `Util.getPreferences()` to use `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context)` instead of the hardcoded filename, making it consistent with the rest of the codebase (`ServerSettingsFragment`, `SettingsFragment`, `getActiveServers()`).

---

## Patch

```diff
--- a/ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java
+++ b/ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java
@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@ public class Util extends DownloadActivity

 	public static SharedPreferences getPreferences(Context context)
 	{
-		return context.getSharedPreferences(Constants.PREFERENCES_FILE_NAME, 0);
+		return PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context);
 	}

 	public static int getRemainingTrialDays(Context context)
```

**File modified:** `ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java` (line 403)

**Why this works:** `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context)` uses the application context to derive the correct preference file name from the actual `applicationId` (including any `.debug` suffix for debug builds), ensuring `getPreferences()` returns the same `SharedPreferences` instance that `ServerSettingsFragment` writes to.

